    1. Choose a marker pattern as a set of 1-3 (near_row, near_col) pairs, each 1-2
    2. Choose 3-6 distinct non-bg base colors + 1 marker color + bg=4
    3. Pick the plain rect size (h_p, w_p); build the output by placing marker pixels at edge-relative positions
    4. For each marked rect, pick a size >= (2*max_near+1) in each dim; stamp the same edge-relative marker pattern onto base color fill
    5. Ensure exactly 2 marked rects overlap the plain rect's row span; others do not
    6. Lay out all rects on a grid with 1-cell bg gaps between neighbors and 1-cell border, sizing the grid to fit
